## Summary of Link and Long-Press Handling in Harmonic for Hacker News

Based on my thorough analysis of the Android project, here are all the code locations related to link handling and long-press menu functionality:

### 1. CUSTOM TEXTVIEW CLASS

**File:** `/Volumes/Dumpy/Research/automated_program_repair_for_ui_bugs/runs/claude_original_run1/bug-114/app/src/main/java/org/sufficientlysecure/htmltextview/HtmlTextView.java`

- **Class:** `HtmlTextView extends JellyBeanSpanFixTextView` (lines 33-181)
- **Key methods:**
  - `setHtml(String html, Html.ImageGetter imageGetter)` - Lines 100-115
    - Sets `LocalLinkMovementMethod.getInstance()` at line 114 to enable link clicking
  - `setOnClickATagListener()` - Lines 137-139 (allows custom link click handling)

**Parent class:** `/Volumes/Dumpy/Research/automated_program_repair_for_ui_bugs/runs/claude_original_run1/bug-114/app/src/main/java/org/sufficientlysecure/htmltextview/JellyBeanSpanFixTextView.java`

- **Class:** `JellyBeanSpanFixTextView extends AppCompatTextView` (lines 47-213)
- Handles span-related rendering fixes for older Android versions

---

### 2. CUSTOM MOVEMENTMETHOD

**File:** `/Volumes/Dumpy/Research/automated_program_repair_for_ui_bugs/runs/claude_original_run1/bug-114/app/src/main/java/org/sufficientlysecure/htmltextview/LocalLinkMovementMethod.java`

- **Class:** `LocalLinkMovementMethod extends LinkMovementMethod` (lines 31-80)
- **Key method:** `onTouchEvent(TextView widget, Spannable buffer, MotionEvent event)` - Lines 42-79
  - Handles touch events on clickable text (lines 45-46: ACTION_UP and ACTION_DOWN)
  - Finds ClickableSpans at touch location (line 60)
  - Calls `link[0].onClick(widget)` when a link is clicked (line 64)
  - Returns `true` when a link is handled, allowing proper event consumption

---

### 3. COMMENTS ADAPTER/VIEWHOLDER LONG-CLICK SETUP

**File:** `/Volumes/Dumpy/Research/automated_program_repair_for_ui_bugs/runs/claude_original_run1/bug-114/app/src/main/java/com/simon/harmonichackernews/CommentsRecyclerViewAdapter.java`

**Inner class:** `ItemViewHolder` (lines 406-447)

- **Long-click on entire comment item** - Lines 423-426:
  ```java
  itemView.setOnLongClickListener(v -> {
      commentLongClickListener.onItemClick(comment, getAbsoluteAdapterPosition(), v);
      return true;
  });
  ```

- **Long-click on comment body (HtmlTextView)** - Lines 428-431:
  ```java
  commentBody.setOnLongClickListener(v -> {
      commentLongClickListener.onItemClick(comment, getAbsoluteAdapterPosition(), v);
      return true;
  });
  ```

- **Regular click on comment body** - Lines 436-437:
  ```java
  commentBody.setOnClickListener(v ->
          commentClickListener.onItemClick(comment, getAbsoluteAdapterPosition(), v));
  ```

- **Link click listener for URLs in comment text** - Lines 439-445:
  ```java
  commentBody.setOnClickATagListener(new OnClickATagListener() {
      @Override
      public boolean onClick(View widget, String spannedText, @Nullable String href) {
          Utils.openLinkMaybeHN(widget.getContext(), href);
          return true;
      }
  });
  ```

**HeaderViewHolder** (lines 449-614)

- **Link click listener for story header text** - Lines 570-576:
  ```java
  textView.setOnClickATagListener(new OnClickATagListener() {
      @Override
      public boolean onClick(View widget, String spannedText, @Nullable String href) {
          Utils.launchCustomTab(mView.getContext(), href);
          return true;
      }
